ok    Runtime starts              msb 0.7.7-puddle.2 (0.0 s)
ok    Test boot                   a test VM booted and ran a program in 1.1 s
ok    Disk space                  120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
warn  Disk encryption             data drive encrypted (x); swap /dev/dm-1 NOT encrypted
      impact: Secrets Puddle holds in memory can be written to swap, where anyone who gets the
              disk can read them.
      remedy: Run `fsutil behavior set encryptpagingfile 1` as administrator, then restart.
      note:   The swap is not encrypted. Puddle keeps secrets in memory while it runs (the real
              values behind the stand-ins a workspace holds), and memory can be paged out to swap
              or written to disk in a crash dump. Anyone who gets this disk (a lost or stolen
              computer, a disk taken out) can read those pages and the data folder. Turn on
              BitLocker or Device encryption for the drive (Settings, Privacy & security, Device
              encryption; Pro editions: Control Panel, BitLocker Drive Encryption). To encrypt the
              page file as well, run `fsutil behavior set encryptpagingfile 1` as administrator,
              then restart.
ok    SSH agent                   the agent on \\.\pipe\openssh-ssh-agent holds 2 keys (ed25519: 1, rsa: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)              version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store            the operating system's credential store: a test write and delete worked
ok    Known problematic software  none found

